# The Go build context is the repository root. OLD/ is the archived Node app,
# kept only as a rollback target, so it is excluded to keep the build context
# small — nothing in the Go image needs it.
#
# The Node image is built with OLD/ as its own context and uses OLD/.dockerignore.
OLD
node_modules
dev-config
dev-data
dev-config-gen.js
.git

# Runtime volumes. Anchored, like .gitignore, and for a sharper reason: the
# build embeds web/templates and web/static via //go:embed. A reader who
# assumed these bare names match at any depth — as .gitignore does — would
# "tidy" them into excluding the embedded assets, and the failure would be a
# confusing compile error rather than a clear missing path.
#
# Docker happens to treat a bare pattern as root-anchored, so these were never
# wrong in practice. They are anchored so the file says what it means.
/config
/data
/templates
/docs
/scripts

# Not needed in any image.
ca_profile.xml
*.md
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile.node
# The Node entrypoint. The Go image uses docker-entrypoint-go.sh, which must
# stay in the context.
docker-entrypoint.sh